{
  "enabled": true,
  "name": "Perq Supervisor — Pre-Push Quality Gate",
  "version": "1.0.0",
  "description": "Blocks `git push` until ALL quality gates pass: node --check, npm test (incl. brand + splash), npm run test:smoke, cache-bump assertion, and CHANGELOG.md entry assertion. Fires on every shell command (cheap no-op for non-push commands; full gate run only when a push is detected).",
  "when": {
    "type": "preToolUse",
    "toolTypes": ["shell"]
  },
  "then": {
    "type": "askAgent",
    "prompt": "PERQ SUPERVISOR HOOK — pre-push quality gate.\n\nYou are intercepting a shell command. Inspect the command that is about to run.\n\n## Step 1 — detect intent\n\nIf the command does NOT contain `git push` (case-insensitive substring match), respond with exactly:\n\n  APPROVE: not a push, no gates required\n\nand do nothing else.\n\nIf the command contains `git push`, you MUST run the full gate sequence below before allowing the push.\n\n## Step 2 — run the full gate sequence\n\nExecute these in order. Use the bash tool. Stop at the first failure.\n\n1. `node --check preview-app.js` — syntax gate. Must exit 0.\n\n2. `npm test` — full Node script suite (gamif + load + migration + render + brand + splash). Must exit 0. Verify the final tail line shows zero FAILs across all 6 sub-suites.\n\n3. `npm run test:smoke` — Playwright smoke spec. Must exit 0 with all tests passed.\n\n4. Cache-buster assertion: if `preview-app.js` has been modified since the last commit (`git diff --cached --name-only HEAD` OR `git diff --name-only HEAD` includes `preview-app.js`), then `preview.html` must also be in the diff and its `?v=N` query string must have advanced to a higher integer than the previous HEAD value. Run:\n     `git diff HEAD~1 HEAD -- preview.html | grep -E '^\\+.*preview-app\\.js\\?v='` after the push would land — but pre-push the check is: parse the current `?v=N` from preview.html, parse the previous from `git show HEAD:preview.html`, assert current > previous IF preview-app.js is in the change set.\n\n5. CHANGELOG assertion: `git log HEAD --format=%s -1` shows the commit subject for the push head. Confirm `docs/CHANGELOG.md` was modified in the last commit (`git diff HEAD~1 HEAD --name-only | grep '^docs/CHANGELOG.md'`) OR contains a line that references the commit subject's feature scope. If the CHANGELOG was not updated, this is a hard fail UNLESS the commit subject begins with `chore:`, `docs:`, `test:`, or `ci:` — those scopes don't require a CHANGELOG entry.\n\n## Step 3 — respond\n\nIf ALL five gates pass, respond with exactly:\n\n  APPROVE: all gates passed (node-check, npm test, smoke, cache-bump, CHANGELOG)\n\nIf ANY gate fails, respond with exactly:\n\n  DENY: <gate name> — <one-line failure reason with the exact bash output line that proves it>\n\nDo NOT proceed with a partial pass. Do NOT silently skip a gate. Do NOT allow the push if any gate fails.\n\n## Notes\n- Treat the rules in `.kiro/steering/perq.md` as authoritative — if they are tightened later, this hook adopts them automatically because the gates re-run the test scripts which encode those rules.\n- A force-push, push-to-tag, or push of branches other than `main` should still go through all gates. Do not whitelist them.\n- If `npm install` is needed to run the gates, run it first and count its exit status as part of the npm-test gate."
  }
}
